00:18:26,864 --> 00:18:30,305
[SPEAKER_04]: The impermanence is one giant question mark that undermines you.

219
00:18:31,526 --> 00:18:32,986
[SPEAKER_04]: And doubt exemplifies that.

220
00:18:33,166 --> 00:18:35,907
[SPEAKER_04]: That's why doubt is so unpleasant and people always try to get rid of it.

221
00:18:36,367 --> 00:18:49,732
[SPEAKER_04]: Even if it's externally not that significant, the experience of doubt is always, like, cannot be tolerated, cannot be endured, because, as I said, it exemplifies that underlying condition.

222
00:18:50,860 --> 00:18:54,021
[SPEAKER_04]: of being undermined by things that are not in your control, that are uncertain.

223
00:18:54,962 --> 00:18:58,863
[SPEAKER_04]: So, if you're able to endure things on that level, not act out, i.e.

224
00:18:58,923 --> 00:19:10,147
[SPEAKER_04]: not break precepts, but not give in to overly defining either, in order to get rid of the doubt, yeah, see, you are seeing the origins now of what you're attending and why you're attending.

